<h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>

<p dir="auto">Update Device Memory docs:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The APR rounds, not "rounds down"</li>
<li>The limits may differ per browser</li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>

<p dir="auto">The first point was just wrong.</p>
<p dir="auto">And we recently update the spec to allow for these to change: <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3543735086" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/w3c/device-memory/issues/50" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/w3c/device-memory/issues/50/hovercard" href="https://github.com/w3c/device-memory/issues/50">w3c/device-memory#50</a></p>
<p dir="auto">Chrome is changing these limits in Chrome 146</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>

<p dir="auto"><a href="https://chromestatus.com/feature/6330376953921536" rel="nofollow">https://chromestatus.com/feature/6330376953921536</a></p>
